    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d724">

                <pb facs="1106" n="1090" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg1090"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/5–2849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Legation in
                        Switzerland </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d724-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-04T14:00:00-04:00">June 4, 1949—2 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Unpal 133. For USDel, Lausanne. For your info only, since USG regards refugee
                    problem as overriding factor in determining eventual disposition Gaza strip
                    (Palun 174 May 28), USG would approve incorporation area in Israel as part final
                    territorial settlement provided this cld be achieved by negot with and full
                    consent Egyptian Govt and provided territorial compensation made to Egypt
                    according Pres’ formula if Egypt desires such compensation. Event transfer to
                    Israel, USG considers fol provisions wld be essential to safeguard refugees and
                    residents Gaza strip: (1) clear and unequivocal assurances by Israeli Govt
                    concerning acceptance refugees and resident population Gaza strip as legitimate
                    cits Israel with same rights and same protection accorded Jewish cits, and
                    Israeli Govt undertaking that its civil and military authorities will respect
                    spirit and letter of such assurances; (2) provision for UN supervision of
                    transfer of area and of subsequent status and treatment of population for
                    appropriate period of time.</p>
                <p>In opinion Emb Cairo (Palun 181 June 2) without consulting Egyptian auths, Egypt
                    might well be willing cede Gaza strip to <pb facs="1107" n="1091"
                        xml:id="pg1091"/> Israel provided latter assumes refugee burden, since area
                    wld ultimately become administrative and financial liability to Egypt. Azzam
                        Pasha<anchor n="2" xml:id="d724-f2"/> (Cairo A–565 May 16<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d724-f3"/> rptd you) expressed similar views. Emb considers it
                    probable Egyptian Govt wld reserve final decision until formal peace negots and
                    wld use as bargaining point.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
